    - no two objects (src/blocker/passthrough) overlap; min gap >= 1 cell
    - objects may touch grid edges (blockers and passthrough often do)
    - yellow (4) absent from input
  output_rule: |
    From each source row, cast horizontal rays left & right; from each source col, cast vertical rays up & down.
    Rays paint non-source, non-blue cells yellow (4). A ray stops before any blue (1) cell or at the grid edge.
    Source and blockers are unchanged; red cells in ray paths become yellow.

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (ray-casting output is deterministic from input; no inverse needed)
