    1. Pick grid 19 rows x 18-19 cols.
    2. Place source (8) rectangle 4-7 x 4-7, centered roughly upper-center with >= 4 gap to all edges.
    3. Place 1-4 blue blockers as solid rectangles. Each must overlap the source's row-band XOR col-band so it actually blocks rays. Vary coverage (partial).
    4. Place 2-6 red passthrough rectangles scattered around the grid. Some should lie in ray paths (overlapping source row/col bands) so they get painted yellow. Ensure no object overlaps.
    5. Verify no two objects overlap (gap >= 1) and yellow (4) is absent.
